# Python bytecode from the mac build tooling
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# isolated verification instance data (PORT=3100)
.verify-*/

# Webdev and review data directories. These hold `.master-key` and the desk SQLite file, so an
# untracked one is a `git add -A` away from a committed wrap key. `.webdev-data*` also covers the
# dated backups (`.webdev-data.bak-20260921/`). See docs/internal/security-register.md, SR-02.
.webdev-data*/
.dpsbuddy-review/

# The `data/` list above is an allowlist of names, so every new file the product writes under it is
# tracked by default. These three were: the portal session that AGENTS.md has said "never commit"
# since Phase 1, the meeting recordings, and the unpacked native components. See SR-19.
data/session.enc
data/meetings/
data/components/

# Review-harness secrets and TLS material. `scripts/review-instance.ps1` writes review.env under
# $HOME and `scripts/review-proxy.mjs` generates its key pair there, but `--cert-dir` takes any
# path, so the repo refuses the file rather than trusting the flag.
review.env
*.pem
